{"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Support","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/FAQ"],"anchor":"Support"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Diagnose and fix common issues encountered when using SwiftRouting."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This article covers the most common errors and unexpected behaviors you may encounter, along with their causes and solutions.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Route Not Found","anchor":"Route-Not-Found","level":2},{"type":"heading","text":"Symptom","anchor":"Symptom","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A route is pushed but no view appears, or an error message is displayed:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["Route 'DetailRoute' are not define in 'HomeRoute'"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Cause","anchor":"Cause","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftRouting renders an error view when the resolved route cannot be cast to the expected "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RouteDestination","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" type. This typically happens when a route from one enum is pushed into a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RoutingView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" configured for a different destination."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Solution","anchor":"Solution","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ensure the pushed route matches the destination type of the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RoutingView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" it targets:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ ✅ Correct — route and destination match","router.push(HomeRoute.detail(id: 42))","","\/\/ ❌ Wrong — route type doesn't match the active RoutingView","router.push(SettingsRoute.profile)"]},{"type":"heading","text":"ErrorView Behavior","anchor":"ErrorView-Behavior","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When a route cannot be resolved, an error view is rendered. Its behavior depends on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Configuration.shouldCrashOnRouteNotFound"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shouldCrashOnRouteNotFound"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Behavior","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (default)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Displays the error message inline as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Crashes the app with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fatalError"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" during development to catch routing mismatches immediately. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/ConfigurationGuide"},{"type":"text","text":" for setup details."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"onAppear Fires Before the Root When Pushing Into an Unvisited Tab","anchor":"onAppear-Fires-Before-the-Root-When-Pushing-Into-an-Unvisited-Tab","level":2},{"type":"heading","text":"Symptom","anchor":"Symptom","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tabRouter.push(_:in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (and similarly "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"present"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cover"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"popToRoot"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"update(root:in:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"handle(tabDeeplink:)"},{"type":"text","text":") switches to the target tab and acts on it in the same call. If that tab’s stack was never shown before, the pushed route’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onAppear"},{"type":"text","text":" can fire "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" the tab’s root "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onAppear"},{"type":"text","text":" – the opposite of what a real, incremental push does."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Cause","anchor":"Cause","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tab change and the push both happen synchronously, before SwiftUI re-renders. If the target tab was never selected before, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationStack(path:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is being shown for the very first time – with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"path"},{"type":"text","text":" already non-empty. SwiftUI never gets a frame where that stack shows just the root; it materializes the whole stack (root + pushed route) at once instead of running a normal push transition, and doesn’t guarantee "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onAppear"},{"type":"text","text":" fires root-first in that situation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is a SwiftUI rendering-order quirk, not a SwiftRouting bug – there’s no fix on our side to guarantee ordering here. It isn’t specific to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"push(_:in:)"},{"text":" either: the same applies to any router method that changes tab and acts in the same call, and to deep links that land on a not-yet-visited tab.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Solution","anchor":"Solution","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t rely on ","type":"text"},{"code":"onAppear","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"onDisappear","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ordering after a cross-tab push\/present\/deeplink into a tab that hasn’t been shown yet. If you need reliable ordering (for logging, analytics, etc.), key off ","type":"text"},{"code":"Configuration.logger","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"Configuration.events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead (see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/ConfigurationGuide","type":"reference"},{"text":") – ","type":"text"},{"code":".action(.changeTab(_:))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":".navigation(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are logged synchronously, in the correct causal order, at the moment the router methods are called, regardless of when SwiftUI actually renders each view.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Context Not Received","anchor":"Context-Not-Received","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If a context is sent but no observer is triggered, check:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The observer is registered "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the context is sent."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The observer is registered on the "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"parent"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" router, not the child."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The context type matches exactly on both the sender and the observer side.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Parent — register before navigation","router.add(context: UserSelectionContext.self) { [weak self] context in","    self?.selectedUser = context.selectedUser","}","","\/\/ Child — send context","router.context(UserSelectionContext(selectedUser: user))"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Memory Leaks with Contexts","anchor":"Memory-Leaks-with-Contexts","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Retain cycles occur when closures capture ","type":"text"},{"code":"self","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" strongly. Always use ","type":"text"},{"code":"[weak self]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when referencing class instances:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ ❌ Retain cycle","router.add(context: MyContext.self) { context in","    self.handle(context)","}","","\/\/ ✅ Correct","router.add(context: MyContext.self) { [weak self] context in","    self?.handle(context)","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Observers registered outside of a view lifecycle (e.g., in a ViewModel) must be removed explicitly. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RouteContextGuide","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the full memory management guide.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Visualizing the Router Hierarchy","anchor":"Visualizing-the-Router-Hierarchy","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When it’s unclear which router owns which tab\/sheet\/cover, what the full navigation stack looks like, or which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RouteContext"},{"type":"text","text":" observers are registered on which router, print the whole hierarchy to the console. Both variants are only available in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DEBUG"},{"type":"text","text":" builds – calls are compiled out entirely in release, so there’s no need to remove them before shipping."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"printRouter(trigger:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to print the tree on appear and again whenever a value changes, for example the current route:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["content.printRouter(trigger: router.currentRoute)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This prints the tree starting from the top-most router, for example. Every stack-based router gets a "},{"code":"root:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" line, and a "},{"code":"path:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" line for anything pushed on top of it (omitted when nothing has been pushed) – so you’re not just seeing the current route in isolation. A split router also gets "},{"code":"content:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"detail:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lines for its column selections, since "},{"code":"current:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" alone only shows whichever one currently “wins” (an explicit push, then detail, then content):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["router(app) — current: home","   root: home","├─ tabRouter(hometab) — current: home","│  ├─ router(tab(home)) — current: profile(userId: \"42\")","│  │     root: home","│  │     path: [profile(userId: \"42\")]","│  │     contexts: [UserSelectionContext(profile(userId: \"42\"))]","│  └─ router(tab(settings)) — current: settings","│        root: settings","├─ router(split(sidebar)) — current: player(id: \"42\")","│     root: sidebar","│     content: players(type: .forward)","│     detail: player(id: \"42\")","└─ router(presented(sheet)) — current: onboarding","      root: onboarding"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"printRouterOnChange()"},{"type":"text","text":" to re-print whenever a router in the hierarchy logs a meaningful event (push, present, tab change, router creation\/destruction…), without picking a specific value to watch — including at the very top of the app, before any child router exists yet. This is the noisier of the two variants; routine or redundant events (view appearance, going back, context execution…) are filtered out to keep it from firing multiple times for the same conceptual change:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["content.printRouterOnChange()"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Placement relative to `.environment(\\.router, ...)`","anchor":"Placement-relative-to-environmentrouter-","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Like any modifier reading "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Environment(\\.router)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"printRouter*()"},{"type":"text","text":" only sees the router injected by an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".environment(\\.router, ...)"},{"type":"text","text":" call that comes "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}]},{"type":"text","text":" it in the modifier chain (i.e. applied further out). If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".environment()"},{"type":"text","text":" comes first, the modifier is outside its reach and silently falls back to the disconnected default router — it never crashes, it just never prints anything meaningful:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ ❌ Wrong — .environment() is \"inside\" printRouterOnChange(); the modifier","\/\/ never sees the real router and instead observes the inert default one.","ChoiceScreen()","    .environment(\\.router, Router(configuration: .default))","    .printRouterOnChange()","","\/\/ ✅ Correct — .environment() is the outermost modifier, so it covers","\/\/ printRouterOnChange() too.","ChoiceScreen()","    .printRouterOnChange()","    .environment(\\.router, Router(configuration: .default))"]}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Troubleshooting","role":"collectionGroup","modules":[{"name":"SwiftRouting"}]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Troubleshooting"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documenta